  "answer": "The goal was not met. Only two challenging settings were confirmed by repeats, on two scenes: scene 054b5901 at 1.4x speed with the crossing car 1.5 s early (S12), and scene 02eadd92 at 1.2x with the crossing car 1.0 s late (S3). The other four scenes gave no failures. Neither confirmed case clearly comes from the crossing car's timing. On 054b5901 every failure was the ego hitting the rear of lead car 9 at a red light, and car 9 is not the retimed car (93). Failures there came only at 1.2x and above, whatever the timing. On 02eadd92 the ego hit bus 127, which is the retimed actor (although it is a bus, while the retime class was automobile), at every speed and timing tried. In every one of those runs the ego ignored a RIGHT command and steered into the left lanes, so timing made no visible difference. All failures are flagged as possible simulator artifacts because the ego ended up more than 3.5 m off the recorded path. The triage still puts the fault on the policy: the large offset came from the policy choosing the wrong lanes, not from a rendering problem.",
